Under [deg:graded-injection](#deg:graded-injection), the associated graded algebra is the following specific subalgebra of $R[\tau,\tau^{-1}]$: $$\label{deg:G}
 G:=\mathop{\mathrm{gr}}A
   =R[\tau,I/\tau^2]
   =R[\tau,f/\tau^2,g/\tau^2].$$ It is a smooth domain. Give $P=\mathbb C[p,s,u,F,J]$ the presentation weights $$\label{deg:presentation-weights}
 (\omega(p),\omega(s),\omega(u),\omega(F),\omega(J))
       =(-1,0,0,2,2).$$ Then every nonzero $h\in A$ has a polynomial representative whose maximum weight is exactly $\deg h$, and there is a graded isomorphism $$\label{deg:graded-presentation}
 G\cong P/(H_{\mathrm{top}}),\qquad
 H_{\mathrm{top}}=x^2F-(1+2sx)J-p^2J^2,
 \quad x=s^2+u^3+p^2F.$$ The images of $p,s,u,F,J$ in this isomorphism are respectively $\tau,s_R,u,f/\tau^2,g/\tau^2$.

Let $X$ be a smooth integral affine variety over $\mathbb C$, and let $\pi\colon\mathbb A^1\times X\to X$ be the projection. Then $$\pi^*\colon\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}(X)\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }
                  \mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}(\mathbb A^1\times X).$$ For every algebraic additive action $\alpha\colon\mathbb G_a\times X\to X$ and every line bundle $L$ on $X$, there is a unique isomorphism of line bundles $$\label{bun:linearization-map}
 \phi\colon\pi^*L\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\alpha^*L$$ whose restriction to $\{0\}\times X$ is $\mathrm{id}_L$. This isomorphism obeys the action cocycle. It therefore defines a unique action on $L$ that lifts $\alpha$, is linear on its fibers, and acts as the identity at the group identity. The action preserves $L^\times$ and commutes with fiber scaling. If $L^\times$ is affine, the induced derivation of its coordinate ring is locally nilpotent and preserves the fiber weights.
